# Defence in depth. The primary pin is publishConfig["@lightlysaltedhq:registry"] in
# package.json, which is the only setting that overrides a scope redirect — a scope-level
# registry beats publishConfig.registry and an explicit --registry flag alike.
#
# This file governs the other direction: what npm LOOKS UP from this directory, for an
# install or a `npm view`, rather than where it publishes. The repository root's .npmrc
# maps the whole @lightlysaltedhq scope to GitHub Packages, correctly, because the root
# package is private and publishes there — and a scope line routes every package in the
# scope, this public one included.
@lightlysaltedhq:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
